you come down that red carpet with all  the flashbulbs and the shouting and the  questions about the dress and you forget  that the only wardrobe choices that  really matter are the five that we're  about to see they are the best costumes  of the year drawn from several decades  by five brilliant designers almost  culinary confections themselves the  delectable designs of nominee Gabriella  Pascucci were a visual feast for  moviegoers in Charlie and the Chocolate  Factory the colorful kimonos and customs  of an era long gone were the inspiration  for the costumes created by nominee  Colleen Atwood and Memoirs of a Geisha  some of the actresses wore nothing at  all but nominee Sandy Powell kept the  rest of the cast well covered in 40s era  costumes for mrs. Henderson presents  novelist Jane Austen herself would  surely nod with approval at the 18th  century British apparel created by  nominee Jacqueline Duran for Pride and  Prejudice  just like his music the life and loves  of Johnny Cash were full of fireworks  and so were the costumes created by  nominee Ariane Phillips or walk the line  and the Oscar goes to Colleen Atwood  Memoirs of a Geisha  this is the second Academy Award and  sixth nomination for Colleen f-word she  took home her first Oscar for Chicago  thank you all very much so many people  to to thank for making this film it was  an effort that circled the globe and  came together here in Los Angeles thanks  to Sony Pictures who were brave enough  to make a movie about a woman fantastic  thank you very much - Rob Marshall my  fantastic director whose vision I only  share to my amazing daughters who are  with me here tonight to my team of  people who really kept it together for  me Sheryl Christine and Colleen and to  the most beautiful cast anybody could  ever dream of dressing and most of all  to the people of Japan who gave me so  much knowledge and grace thank you
 

